      "text": "{\"verdicts\":[{\"n\":1,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:58-59\"],\"reason\":\"escape_silent returns `Markup()` for None, which is the empty Markup string.\"},{\"n\":2,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:7-10\"],\"reason\":\"The module tries `from ._speedups import _escape_inner` and falls back to `._native` on ImportError.\"},{\"n\":3,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:133-134\"],\"reason\":\"`__html__` simply returns `self`.\"},{\"n\":4,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:303-311\"],\"reason\":\"Both partition methods call `super().partition(sep)`/`rpartition(sep)` with the separator unescaped.\"},{\"n\":5,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:173-186\"],\"reason\":\"Each of split, rsplit, splitlines returns `[self.__class__(v) for v in ...]`.\"},{\"n\":6,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:228\"],\"reason\":\"The final statement of striptags is exactly `return self.__class__(value).unescape()`.\"},{\"n\":7,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:235-240\"],\"reason\":\"It checks `if rv.__class__ is not cls: return cls(rv)` and otherwise returns `rv` unchanged.\"},{\"n\":8,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:242-243\"],\"reason\":\"`__getitem__` returns `self.__class__(super().__getitem__(key))`.\"},{\"n\":9,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:212-224\"],\"reason\":\"Both loops break when the closing `-->` or `>` is not found, leaving the remaining text intact.\"},{\"n\":10,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:84-330\",\"CHANGES.rst:55-59\"],\"reason\":\"Markup does not override `__contains__`, `find`, or `index`, so they use the plain str behavior with no escaping.\"},{\"n\":11,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/_speedups.c:83-87\"],\"reason\":\"When `delta` is zero the code does `Py_INCREF(in)` and returns the input object itself.\"},{\"n\":12,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:136-138\"],\"reason\":\"`__add__` builds `super().__add__(self.escape(value))`.\"},{\"n\":13,\"label\":\"contradicted\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/_speedups.c:3-16\",\"src/markupsafe/_speedups.c:83-96\"],\"reason\":\"The C code makes two passes: GET_DELTA first scans the input to compute the size, then DO_ESCAPE writes to the new buffer.\"},{\"n\":14,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:212-224\"],\"reason\":\"Both the comment-stripping and tag-stripping loops use `value.find(...)` with no regex.\"},{\"n\":15,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/_native.py:2-8\"],\"reason\":\"The chained replaces occur in exactly the order &, >, <, ', \\\".\"},{\"n\":16,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:39-45\"],\"reason\":\"Every return path of the module-level escape constructs `Markup(...)`, not a subclass.\"},{\"n\":17,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:266-276\"],\"reason\":\"strip, lstrip and rstrip pass `chars` straight to the str implementations without escaping.\"},{\"n\":18,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:325-329\"],\"reason\":\"`__html_format__` raises only for a non-empty spec and otherwise returns `self`.\"},{\"n\":19,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:136-138\"],\"reason\":\"The result of `super().__add__` is wrapped with `self.__class__`, preserving subclasses.\"},{\"n\":20,\"label\":\"supported\",\"lines\":[\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:39-40\",\"src/markupsafe/__init__.py:128-129\"],\"reason\":\"Even when `_escape_inner` returns the identical str, `Markup(...)` unconditionally calls `super().__new__(cls, object)`, producing a new Markup instance.\"}]}",
